et update && apt-get install -y unzip` (Debian, Ubuntu), `dnf install -y unzip` (Fedora, RHEL) or `apk add unzip` (Alpine), with `sudo` in front unless you are root. No way to install packages? Use the no-unzip route, not an improvised one. > > `gbrain setup --instructions-only` tells the agent the brain is there; agents seldom call an MCP server nobody told them about. It writes the brain-first block into `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` or Codex's `AGENTS.md` (a non-empty `AGENTS.override.md` instead when Codex has one) with a per-turn rule hook, and leaves the MCP entry alone; the same command with `--no-instructions` added takes them out. > > The installer is a shell script for macOS and Linux; read it before you run it. ### Here's how to self-host it GBrain is MIT-licensed and free to self-host. It needs **Bun 1.4.4 or newer**; existing worker installs read the authorization and queue upgrade guide before restarting on this version. > [!WARNING] > **GBrain is NOT distributed on npm.** The npm `gbrain` package is unrelated and > can shadow the real binary, so never run `npm install -g gbrain` or > `bun add -g gbrain`. Install only via `bun install -g github:garrytan/gbrain#stable` > (the soaked stable channel; `#latest-stable` is the alpha line with every release) > or `git clone --branch stable` + `bun install && bun link`. Installed by mistake? `gbrain doctor` gives the fix. > Schema not migrated (#218)? Run > `gbrain apply-migrations --yes --no-autopilot-install`; if it exits 1, run `gbrain doctor --json`, not another `--yes` (`wedged`: relay its fix). ```bash bun install -g github:garrytan/gbrain#stable gbrain setup claude-code              # or: gbrain setup codex gbrain init --pglite --no-embedding   # any other harness, or no agent ``` `gbrain setup` shows what it will write first (`--dry-run` previews, `--remove` undoes), creates a keyless brain only if none exists, wires MCP, hooks and a brain-first block in the agent's instruction file (`--no-instructions` skips 